From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SushyDev <mail@sushy.dev>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:08:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: don't re-decide DSC from the reduced bpp

msm_dp_bridge_mode_set() stages and commits the DSC decision using the
EDID bpp, and msm_dp_panel_commit_dsc() then writes the DSC source bpp
back into msm_dp_mode.bpp.  msm_dp_panel_init_panel_info() re-ran the
same decision against that already-reduced value.

At 3440x1440@120 the two passes disagree.  Against the EDID's 10 bpc,
698750 * 30 = 20.96 Gbps exceeds the 16.87 Gbps budget so DSC is
committed.  Against the reduced 24 bpp, 698750 * 24 = 16.77 Gbps fits,
so the second pass cleared dsc_en after the DPU had already latched the
compressed topology.  The DPU then compresses into a transmitter that is
not decompressing.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
index bc46e79..1b798ba 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
@@ -1232,9 +1232,11 @@ int msm_dp_panel_init_panel_info(struct msm_dp_panel *msm_dp_panel)
 				drm_mode->clock);
 	drm_dbg_dp(panel->drm_dev, "bpp = %d\n", msm_dp_panel->msm_dp_mode.bpp);
 
-	msm_dp_panel_stage_dsc(msm_dp_panel, drm_mode,
-			msm_dp_panel->msm_dp_mode.bpp);
-	msm_dp_panel_commit_dsc(msm_dp_panel);
+	if (!msm_dp_panel->msm_dp_mode.dsc_en) {
+		msm_dp_panel_stage_dsc(msm_dp_panel, drm_mode,
+				msm_dp_panel->msm_dp_mode.bpp);
+		msm_dp_panel_commit_dsc(msm_dp_panel);
+	}
 	if (!msm_dp_panel->msm_dp_mode.dsc_en)
 		msm_dp_panel->msm_dp_mode.bpp = msm_dp_panel_get_mode_bpp(msm_dp_panel,
 							msm_dp_panel->msm_dp_mode.bpp,
